$image2text — vision-language (Qwen2-VL / Qwen3-VL)

SUMMARY
  Runs a Qwen vision-language model on each images[] file with a prompt and writes
  model text into texts[] (one .txt per image).

SYNTAX
  $image2text
  $image2text(model='qwen3', gpu=True)
  $image2text(model='qwen2', max_tokens=256)
  $image2text(prompt='What bird is this?')

INPUT
  images[]  — source images (PNG, JPG, …)
  prompts[] — optional per-image questions (or instruction body / prompt= arg)

OUTPUT
  texts[] — one text file per image (model response)

ARGUMENTS
  model=      — qwen2 (default) | qwen3; or model=@instruction (one name per texts[] line)
  prompt=     — same prompt for every image (overrides prompts[])
  max_tokens= — generation limit (default 512)
  gpu=        — use CUDA (default: on when torch sees a GPU; gpu=False for CPU)

MODELS
  Default: models/qwen-vl/Qwen2-VL-2B-Instruct/ (~4 GB)
  model=qwen3: models/qwen-vl/Qwen3-VL-8B-Instruct/ (~16 GB+; needs GPU for practical use)
  First run downloads automatically from Hugging Face.

DEPENDENCIES
  Uses .venvs/media (torch + transformers>=4.57). Run tools\setup_external_venvs.ps1 once.
  Or: uv sync --extra media

ENVIRONMENT
  AH_EMULATE_IMAGE2TEXT=1 — placeholder text, no model load.
  AH_IMAGE2TEXT_GPU=0       — force CPU even when CUDA is available.

EXAMPLE
  @photo: $file('garden.jpg') -> $image2text
  What species of bird is in this photo?

  @detail: $file('scene.jpg') -> $image2text(model='qwen3')
  List every object and its approximate position.

PROMPT-CONSUMING
  Yes — prompts[] cleared on output; images[] pass through; input texts[] replaced.
